&lt;p&gt;A virtuosic bassoonist, conductor, and core member of the International Contemporary Ensemble, Rebekah Heller is celebrated for reimagining the bassoon&amp;#39;s possibilities through adventurous performances and groundbreaking commissions. In this Pop-Up Concert, she performs a program of new music for bassoon choir by composers from the African Diaspora, including the world premiere of&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Righteous Rage&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;by Brittany J. Green, which was inspired by and is in direct conversation with another work on the program, Julius Eastman&amp;rsquo;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;The Holy Presence of Joan d&amp;rsquo;Arc&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;(originally for 10 cellos).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
